      ],
      "content": "liere (lioure): tape, or narrow strips of cloth, used for binding the edges of a fabric — for veils, sails, bed-hangings etc. (OED s.v. lear2, lyre2; MED s.v. lioure). The name is associated with Lire/Liere in Brabant."
    }
